        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0205" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg133"/>

                <head>[From the Opinion Nationale, May 1, 1865.]</head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1865-05-01">May 1, 1865</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>We are assured that Mr. W. H. Seward is out of danger, and America may still
                    reckon upon the services of this skilful diplomatist, who is at the same time an
                    honest man.</p>
                <p>It has been remarked that the federal securities have experienced no depreciation
                    in the different markets of the United States. Such is the power of democratic
                    institutions, when they are founded upon ripe judgments, and upon the energy of
                    religious sentiment, which no incident, how lamentable soever, is able to shake
                    by compromising the national credit and the public wealth.</p>
            </div>
